            "id": "q6",
            "type": "subjective",
            "marks": 2,
            "question": "Find the value of $\\frac{\\sqrt{32} + \\sqrt{48}}{\\sqrt{8} + \\sqrt{12}}$.",
            "finalAnswer": "2",
            "solutionSteps": [
                "$\\sqrt{32} = 4\\sqrt{2}$, $\\sqrt{48} = 4\\sqrt{3}$. Numerator = $4(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{3})$.",
                "$\\sqrt{8} = 2\\sqrt{2}$, $\\sqrt{12} = 2\\sqrt{3}$. Denominator = $2(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{3})$.",
                "Ratio = $4/2 = 2$."
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "q7",
            "type": "subjective",
            "marks": 3,
            "question": "If $a$ and $b$ are rational numbers and $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{\\sqrt{3}+1} = a + b\\sqrt{3}$, find $a$ and $b$.",
            "finalAnswer": "a = 2, b = -1",
            "solutionSteps": [
                "Rationalize the LHS: $\\frac{(\\sqrt{3}-1)^2}{(\\sqrt{3}+1)(\\sqrt{3}-1)} = \\frac{3 + 1 - 2\\sqrt{3}}{3 - 1}$",
                "$= \\frac{4 - 2\\sqrt{3}}{2} = 2 - \\sqrt{3}$.",
                "Comparing with $a + b\\sqrt{3}$: $a = 2$, $b = -1$."
            ]
        },
